# exec-todo (Cursor)

Turn a plan/checklist file into actively-tracked, actually-executed work.
Not a planning tool — never edits plan *content*, only checkboxes and file
location.

## Resolve the target file

Exact path if given; otherwise fuzzy-match against this repo's plan-doc
location, preferring an open/unfinished match over a closed one. No
argument at all → ask which file, don't guess. Read the resolved file in
full before doing anything else.

## Build the tracked task list

Extract every unchecked item from the checklist section, in order,
including any fixed closing items this repo requires. One task per session
todo item. If everything's already checked, check whether the file needs
moving to a "done" location per this repo's convention instead of
fabricating work.

## Work through it

Per task: mark in-progress → do the work (multi-step items follow
incremental, small-diff discipline) → verify before marking done → check
off both the session task and the `- [ ]` → `- [x]` in the file in the same
turn. New work discovered mid-implementation gets added as a new item, not
folded silently into an existing one. Surface blockers instead of skipping
past them.

## Closing gates — not optional

Follow this repo's own documented "definition of done" (check
`CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`/`CONTRIBUTING.md` first) exactly, in order. Default
if none exists: dispatch a review step → run real verification (E2E/manual,
not just unit tests) → write whatever report artifact this repo expects →
clean up test state → check off closing items → move the file to its "done"
location if this repo's convention has one, fixing relative links.

## Final report

What was implemented, test/review/verification results, and the file's
final location. Say plainly if anything was left unchecked — never imply
full completion the file itself doesn't show.
